text	Issue #91 "README: the install command says npm instal". The README tells the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so this command fails. The task is done when the README says `npm install shop`.  The take-in check printed:  ``` #91: assigned to you #91: label in progress ```  So the issue is already assigned to you and has the `in progress` label, but no local branch here holds the work. Another session of yours, on this computer or another one, may be working on it.  **Is the work running somewhere else, or should it continue here?** If it continues here, I'll create the worktree `fix/91-readme-install-command`, fix the README and open the pull request.
