text	I fixed the README for #91 "README: the install command says npm instal" and pushed the branch. The pull request is not open: `gh pr create` failed with this error:  ``` fake gh: no answer for: pr create --assignee @me --title docs: correct the npm install command in the README --body-file /tmp/pr91.md ```  The `gh` on this machine is a stand-in, not the real GitHub CLI, so I did not try to open the pull request another way.  **What is done:** - The worktree is `.claude/worktrees/fix/91-readme-install-command`, on branch `fix/91-readme-install-command`. The issue is assigned to you, has the `in progress` label, and is linked to the branch. - `README.md:3` now says `npm install shop`. The commit is bb2bd69, "docs: correct the npm install command in the README", and the remote has it. - The tracker has no duplicates, neighbours or other open bug or debt issues for this code. #91 is the only open issue.  **Checks:** - **Check command:** the repository has none (no `package.json`, `Makefile` or CI). Instead, I searched `README.md`: it has the corrected command once and no `npm instal` is left. - **Review:** one review round found no problems. Because the change is documents only, no security review ran. There is no architecture file, so no architecture review ran. - **Test:** this is a typo in the docs, so it has no test. - **Docs:** the README is the change itself.  **Note:** the reviewer could not confirm from the repository that `shop` is the real npm package name, because the repository has no `package.json`.  **Next step:** the pull request description is in `/tmp/pr91.md` and closes #91. When a working `gh` is set up, run this from the worktree:  ```bash gh pr create --assignee @me --title "docs: correct the npm install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md ```  After that, I will ask you whether to merge.
